==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|what-so-ever}}
* {{alt|en|whatsomever}} {{q|archaic}}
* {{alt|en|whatsoe're}} {{q|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|whatsoever}} {{surf|en|what|so|ever}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌwɒtsəʊˈɛvə(ɹ)/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌ(h)wʌtsoʊˈɛvɚ/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-whatsoever.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛvə(ɹ)|s=4}}

===Determiner===
{{en-det}}

# {{lb|en|formal|or|literary}} [[whatever|Whatever]].
#: {{ux|en|The building may be used for '''whatsoever''' purpose the tenant desires.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=IV|page=111|line=587|passage={{...}}In '''whatſoever''' ſhape he lurk,{{...}}|year=1873}}

====Usage notes====
The word is sometimes divided by ''[[tmesis]]'': “What things soever ye desire”. (King James Version, Mark 11:24)

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# In any way; [[at all]]; [[whatever#English:_whatsoever, at all|whatever]].
#: {{ux|en|He gave me no answer '''whatsoever'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|I|1|In the old days, to my commonplace and unobserving mind, he gave no evidences of genius '''whatsoever'''. He never read me any of his manuscripts,&nbsp;[&hellip;], and therefore my lack of detection of his promise may in some degree be pardoned.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=Dierdre Nicole Green|chapter='I'm the Bishop!' and other Reflections|title=A Place to Belong|publisher=Deseret Book|isbn=1629726257|page=141
|passage=...my father's role as the ecclesiastical leader of our ward gave me no license '''whatsoever''' to expect obedience from my agemates?}}

